<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- The route kit (D'thorga Framework 0.281.0; docs/development/autonomous-vehicles.md, step 7a; the owner's cards of 25 Nov 2026: a
       fitting for any vehicle). Fitted at the vehicle workshop on any vehicle with a D'thorga loadout, on the sensor bar every land vehicle
       has (Loadouts_Default.xml). It grants RouteControl: the vehicle may follow a leader (at most four to one, the owner's) or run a loop
       between two stops, with nobody aboard, and stops when its leader is lost. It draws on the battery and works only with that load on.
       Real basis: the US Army's leader-follower trucks, and the four that followed a crewed leader near Puckapunyal in June 2023. Cost:
       an advanced component for its controller, as the owner chose for the remote control kit; load, weight, work and skill authored.
       It borrows a picture until its own is drawn. Not yet tested in game. -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
    <defName>PhobosFitting_RouteKit</defName>
    <iconPath>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Hitch/Hitch</iconPath>
    <label>route kit</label>
    <description>Cameras and a small radar on a bar over the cab, a controller, and servos on the wheel, pedals and gear lever. With it the vehicle can follow a crewed vehicle in a convoy, or run back and forth between two stops you mark, with nobody aboard. It cannot load or unload itself, go anywhere new or fight; if its leader is lost, it stops. It draws on the battery. The driver's seat stays.</description>
    <roles><li>RouteKitMount</li></roles>
    <materials><Steel>30</Steel><ComponentIndustrial>4</ComponentIndustrial><ComponentSpacer>1</ComponentSpacer></materials>
    <kilograms>20</kilograms>
    <work>3000</work>
    <minSkill>5</minSkill>
    <researchPrerequisite>PhobosResearch_VehicleAutonomy</researchPrerequisite>
    <grants><li>RouteControl</li></grants>
    <loads>
      <li>
        <!-- Cameras, radar, controller and servos at rest: about 3 A at 12 V (authored), halved on a 24 V truck. Shed late: a vehicle that
             loses it stops. -->
        <name>routeKit</name>
        <label>route kit</label>
        <description>The route kit's sensors, controller and servos. With power, the vehicle can follow a leader or run its loop by itself.</description>
        <amps>3</amps>
        <shedOrder>9</shedOrder>
        <iconPath>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Hitch/Hitch</iconPath>
      </li>
    </loads>
    <feed>
      <load>routeKit</load>
    </feed>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
</Defs>
